      "before": null,
      "after": {
        "id": "agr-reader-rice-workrecord-spacing",
        "knowledgeId": "agriculture-v2-AGR-K-RICEWORK-FIELD-05",
        "lessonId": "agr-ricework-field",
        "levels": [
          "1",
          "2"
        ],
        "promptJa": "さぎょうきろくで、たうえきの「6じょう」というじょうすうを、そのままかぶまのすうちとしてうつしてしまいました。じょうすう・じょうかん・かぶまのちがいをつかって、きろくのまちがいをせつめいしましょう。",
        "modelAnswerJa": "育てた苗を田植機で植えるのが移植栽培の田植えです。田植機の条数は一度に植える列の数に関係し、苗の本数や作物の品種名とは別の情報です。\n\n条間は列と列、株間は株と株の間隔です。資料には条間30cmの例があり、株間は田植機で調整すると示されています。株間の記載は1号と2号で異なるため、全水田に共通する一つの設定値として扱いません。",
        "translations": {
          "en": {
            "prompt": "In a work record, the transplanter’s “six rows” was copied directly as the plant-spacing value. Explain the recording error by distinguishing row count, row spacing and plant spacing.",
            "modelAnswer": "In transplant cultivation, raised seedlings are planted with a rice transplanter. The machine’s row count relates to how many rows it plants in one pass; it is different information from the number of seedlings or the crop variety.\n\nRow spacing is the distance between rows; hill spacing is the distance between planted hills. The source gives an example of 30 cm row spacing and states that hill spacing is adjusted on the transplanter. The descriptions of hill spacing differ between the level 1 and level 2 sources, so do not treat them as one universal setting for all paddies.",
            "translatedFrom": "ja"
          },
          "vi": {
